Reports terrain at exactly 0 m under the map center. The renderer started from
a last reported height of 0 m, so it never reported sea-level ground, and a
clamped center over it never learned of the ground: the clamp neither settled
the center there nor lifted an eye under a cliff beside the sea. The height now
starts unknown, and the first report waits for a loaded DEM tile under the
center, so ground that has not loaded yet still does not read as sea level.
Upstream: not proposed

